ony Evers retiring. Polling since summer has consistently placed David Crowley ahead of Tom Tiffany by two to five points, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters, and the most recent reading in early October showed a four-point lead. Prediction markets price Crowley around 80 percent, and several ratings outlets call the race Lean Democratic, though others place it in tossup territory.\n\nThe main counterweight is money: Tiffany has raised roughly ten times what Crowley has, holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, and benefits from a late advertising blitz from a Koch-backed group. Tiffany has also worked to keep his distance from Donald Trump and soften his abortion stance, aiming at swing voters in a state with evenly balanced partisanship. The evidence points to a narrow but genuine Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7127, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7543, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7549, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7589, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.724, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7645, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7536, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7419, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.746, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7525, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7388, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6631, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6796, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6642, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7316, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.696, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7399, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7761, "ma